# Visual spacing debug (MailGent)

**When:** Swift / SwiftUI layout work **and** the bug is **where space sits** (title↔card, scroll-away gap, “too much pad”, “zero the top of X”). Skip for non-Swift UI, and for building a new visual feature from scratch (`ui-inventory.mdc` / HTML feature proto).

## 1. Name layers before editing

Write the layers in chat and get agreement on **which one** changes:

| Layer | Meaning |
|-------|---------|
| **A** | Outside a scroll/stack — e.g. pad under a title **before** the scroll box |
| **B** | Inside scroll/stack content — space **above the first card** that moves when you scroll |
| **C** | Card-internal pad / inter-card `gap` / footer gap (only if named) |

Do **not** code until the target layer is named. User “top of the scrolled box” → **B**; “under the title” → **A**.

## 2. Content tree before AppKit

For anything that **shrinks or vanishes when scrolling**:

1. List the first ~3 views inside the `ScrollView` / stack.
2. If a non-content first child exists (`Color.clear`, spacer, zero-height anchor), treat that + `VStack`/`HStack` **spacing** as the prime suspect — zero-height views still take spacing.
3. One-line differential: remove that child or set top spacing to 0 → dogfood.
4. Only then reach for `contentMargins`, `contentInsets`, or `NSViewRepresentable` clearers.

Prefer **delete / relocate** over AppKit bridges.

## 3. One hypothesis → one dogfood

Do not stack inset-clearer + margin zero + outside-pad remove in one pass. On “still wrong,” **reset**: re-read the layout block cold, restate A/B/C — do not patch the previous patch.

## 4. After one failed try → pointing prototype

If the first focused fix does not match dogfood (or language is already fuzzy), **stop stacking Swift fixes** and propose a **simple** HTML map under `.scratch/<feature>/` (e.g. `spacing-map.html`):

- Same regions as the live UI (title, scroll box, first card, footer) — boxes + short labels (**A** / **B** / …), not a full redesign
- User points (“B is too big”, “keep A”) so chat shares names with the map
- Implement only after that pointing pass (or an explicit “skip proto, just fix B”)

Keep it throwaway and minimal; feature protos / inventory rules still win for new chrome.
